  "order": 50,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "vebv78l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FEATURES OF THE INDIAN CONSTITUTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Constitution of India is the lengthiest written constitution, combining both rigid and flexible amendment procedures.",
        "It establishes a federal system with a unitary bias and a parliamentary form of government.",
        "It guarantees Fundamental Rights, Directive Principles of State Policy, and Fundamental Duties to its citizens.",
        "It provides for an independent judiciary, judicial review, the rule of law, and single citizenship.",
        "It establishes a secular state with universal adult franchise, emergency provisions, and independent constitutional bodies."
      ],
      "id": "nnwg6vb"
    },
